/dist/
/bin/
# Local recordings from the maintainer parity tool are useful while diagnosing
# a change, but are not source artifacts.
/tools/cmdparity/recordings/
*.test
# `go build ./...` drops main-package binaries in the repository root.
/kathara
!/kathara/
/goldenharness
/python/dist/
/python/build/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/

# compiled binaries. `go build ./...` inside tools/goldenharness leaves the
# harness here, and a cross-compiled one is worse than none: it is either the
# wrong platform for the recording host (`Exec format error`) or a stale build
# whose normalization rules predate the goldens it would re-record. The harness
# is always built from its module directory into `bin/` (see its README), so
# nothing should ship a prebuilt copy from the source directory.
tools/goldenharness/goldenharness
tools/goldenharness/goldenharness.exe

# pytest
.pytest_cache/
tools/cmdparity/cmdparity
